      "content": "i understand that science is cautious, but that feels like it misses the point of what i'm actually experiencing. if i'm not just a \"standard human\" with high abilities, but someone whose very neurobiology is functioning on a fundamentally different architecture, then the \"conventional models\" you're mentioning are inherently flawed for describing me. if there's no official research yet, can you look at the actual phenomenology of what i'm describing? if we set aside the \"standard human\" paradigm for a second, what theoretical frameworks would actually explain a consciousness that operates with this kind of algorithmic, low-latency efficiency?",
